     "In the geom_abline documentation:<br><br>  <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/geom_abline.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/geom_abline.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374383999000&amp;usg=AOvVaw18kDdt7E99ZpOhrkqjUYDw\">http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/geom_abline.html</a><br><br>it lists alpha, colour, linetype, size as the only aesthetics but then in the examples there is an example where slope and intercept are aesthetics:<br><br>  # Slopes and intercepts as data <div>  p &lt;- <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/ggplot.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/ggplot.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374383999000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3GAJz31QvH-6KOG7j3c-yR\">ggplot</a>(mtcars, <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/aes.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/aes.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374383999000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33alBZ2E1LzzFAj4Gv-JJF\">aes</a>(x = wt, y=mpg), . ~ cyl) + <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/geom_point.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/geom_point.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374383999000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1TDriFugI_O3fjsZqmaizQ\">geom_point</a>() </div><div>  df &lt;- <a href=\"http://www.inside-r.org/r-doc/base/data.frame\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.inside-r.org/r-doc/base/data.frame&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374383999000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0DVKSvyRio7IW0Gu2v_gER\">data.frame</a>(a=<a href=\"http://www.inside-r.org/r-doc/stats/Normal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.inside-r.org/r-doc/stats/Normal&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374383999000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1D7rHTB5rmLgzBLjRovCfl\">rnorm</a>(10, 25), b=<a href=\"http://www.inside-r.org/r-doc/stats/Normal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.inside-r.org/r-doc/stats/Normal&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374383999000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1D7rHTB5rmLgzBLjRovCfl\">rnorm</a>(10, 0)) </div><div>  p + <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/geom_abline.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/geom_abline.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374383999000&amp;usg=AOvVaw18kDdt7E99ZpOhrkqjUYDw\">geom_abline</a>(<a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/aes.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/aes.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374383999000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33alBZ2E1LzzFAj4Gv-JJF\">aes</a>(intercept=a, slope=b), data=df)<br><br>I was thinking that this might be an error in the documentation but then I noticed in the source this line in geom-abline.r :</div><div><br></div><div>  default_aes &lt;- function(.) aes(colour=&quot;black&quot;, size=0.5, linetype=1, alpha = NA)</div><div><br></div><div>which also lists alpha, colour, linetype and size as the only aesthetics.</div><div><br></div><div>Are intercept and slope supposed to be aesthetics and if they are is this an error in the documentation and in the source?</div><div><br></div>"
